Initial Course Project Plan

Project Goals
The main goal of our project is to explore patterns and trends in U.S. flight delay data using exploratory data analysis (EDA). We want to understand how different factors, such as route, flight distance, and delay type, affect total flight delays. Through this project, we also want to improve our skills in data cleaning, data visualization, collaboration, and statistical communication.
Our group hopes to answer questions such as:
Which types of delays contribute the most to overall delays?
Do longer flights tend to experience larger delays?
Which flight routes appear most frequently and have the highest delays?
In addition to answering these research questions, each team member will create their own visualization and analysis to demonstrate individual contributions and understanding of the data.

Resources Needed
To complete this project successfully, our team will need:
A reliable and detailed dataset with multiple variables
R and RStudio for data analysis and visualization
GitHub for version control and collaboration
Good communication between team members
Clear division of responsibilities
Enough time for both individual and group work
Internet access and documentation resources for troubleshooting

Planned Steps and Responsibilities
1. Choose a Research Topic and Questions (Both Members)
Our team will first decide on a transportation-related topic and create several research questions related to flight delays and airport traffic patterns.
2. Obtain and Understand the Dataset (Both Members)
We will download flight delay data from the U.S. Department of Transportation database and examine the variables, structure, and possible limitations of the data.
3. Clean and Prepare the Data (Shang-Hsuan)
We will remove missing or unnecessary values, create new variables such as total delay and route names, and prepare the data for analysis and visualization.
4. Conduct Exploratory Data Analysis (Both Members)
We will calculate descriptive statistics and explore trends, distributions, and relationships in the dataset.
5. Create Visualizations
Shang-Hsuan will focus on route and delay visualizations(2 graphs).
Tianyu will focus on distance and trend analysis visualizations(1 graph).
Each member will create at least one professional-quality graph and interpret the results.
6. Interpret Results and Discuss Findings (Both Members)
We will compare our findings and discuss possible explanations for the patterns observed in the data.
7. Write the Final Report (mainly Tianyu)
The team will combine all analyses, visualizations (ShangHsuan), explanations, and reflections into a single reproducible QMD report.
8. Prepare the Presentation (Both Members)
We will summarize our research question, findings, and challenges into a short presentation for the class.

Data Source
We are using real-world transportation data from the U.S. Department of Transportation Bureau of Transportation Statistics (BTS).
Data source:
 https://www.transtats.bts.gov/DL_SelectFields.aspx?gnoyr_VQ=FGJ&QO_fu146_anzr=b0-gvzr
